    "section": "reading",
    "skill": "Main idea",
    "q": "Which statement best captures the purpose of the passage?",
    "o": [
      "To evaluate the trial addressing disputes over unattended desks and identify a more informative comparison.",
      "To provide detailed instructions for implementing the change at a university reading room.",
      "To establish that the end of the examination period fully explains the reported observation.",
      "To compare the financial costs of several institutions facing disputes over unattended desks."
    ],
    "e": "Gagasan utama mencakup masalah, hasil percobaan, dan pengujian lanjutan. Petunjuk teknis, kepastian penyebab alternatif, dan perbandingan biaya bukan fokus bacaan.",
    "origin": "original",
    "passage": {
      "id": "SM-DR-R-07",
      "title": "Reading rooms",
      "text": "A team at a university reading room had been concerned about disputes over unattended desks. The team introduced time-limited reservation cards. During a 6-week trial, fewer desk disputes were reported. Staff kept daily logs describing both the operation of the change and the conditions under which it was used. These records were intended to make the experience available for later examination, rather than leave the discussion dependent on the recollection of one unusually successful day.\n\nThe observation did not settle every question about the change. The result could also have been affected by the end of the examination period. A comparison between the period before the change and the period after it would therefore combine two differences: the new procedure and the surrounding conditions. Counting more observations of the same combination would make that combination better described, but would not by itself separate the contributions of its components. The team kept the outcome in the report while distinguishing the observation from a claim about its cause. The first round supplied an observation, and the subsequent round was planned to test its explanation.\n\nThe proposed next investigation was to evaluate the rules during another examination period. The staff would define the outcome in the same way across the comparison and retain records of relevant conditions. A useful question was whether the observed difference would remain when those conditions were made comparable. This question was narrower than deciding whether the procedure was best for every institution, every user, or every future period. The proposed comparison would supply evidence about the specified setting; applying it elsewhere would require considering how that other setting differed."
    },
    "solution": {
      "steps": [
        "Gagasan utama mencakup masalah, hasil percobaan, dan pengujian lanjutan. Petunjuk teknis, kepastian penyebab alternatif, dan perbandingan biaya bukan fokus bacaan."
      ],
      "evidence": "The proposed next investigation was to evaluate the rules during another examination period."
    },
    "difficulty": "foundation",
    "drillOnly": true,
