      "title": "An old timetable",
      "text": "An imaginary island archive contains ferry timetables from two decades. The earlier sheets list departures by village, but the later sheets list them by route.\n\nA curator first reads the change as evidence that village stops disappeared. A surviving ticket, however, names a village on both the earlier and later dates.\n\nThe ticket is a counterexample to the claim that all village stops vanished. It cannot establish how frequently any particular stop was served.\n\nThe curator now treats the new headings as a change in presentation unless further records show operational change. A timetable's categories are evidence about classification as well as transport."
