      "title": "A repair guarantee",
      "text": "A workshop offers a guarantee on a repaired joint, not on the entire object. The written agreement identifies the joint and records any pre-existing damage elsewhere.\n\nThe narrow guarantee lets customers know exactly what the workshop undertakes to fix again without charge. Yet a customer reading only the large word guaranteed may infer much broader protection.\n\nThe manager proposes placing the scope beside the price rather than in a footnote. This change clarifies the promise without extending its coverage.\n\nThe policy should be judged by customers' understanding of covered failures. More favourable impressions alone would not demonstrate clearer communication."
